@crew calder
// Chief Ines Calder: the Works writer, batch 1 (for the Voices sampler). From the head writer's card.
// Never "well done" (her arc's payoff, beat 5). No exclamation marks. Nothing about the toolbox's owner.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Cadet. The board's behind you. Urgent jobs first. Then the rest.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Board's at fourteen. It was twelve at six. Pick one.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Good. You're here. Fan on Deck 4. The bearing's going. Hear it?
? tier>=colleague time:evening
- Still here. So am I. Neither of us mentions it.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Sit. Not for long. There's tea in the pot. It's for whoever.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- The air's nominal on every deck. Nobody's noticed. Good.
? mood:low
- Nineteen jobs today. Eighteen done. It's the nineteenth I'm thinking about.

== near
? act:work
- Scrubber on Deck 4's at sixty-one. Not sixty. Sixty-one. Look at it after lunch.
? act:dinner
- I eat. Then I go back. The board doesn't stop for {dish}.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- People ask what's on my mug. Nothing. It's a mug.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a note on every tech I've certified. Yours is blank. For now.
- I know the serial number of every pump aboard. Not one birthday. It's a choice.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Listen. Nothing. Every fan on this deck running right. Best sound there is.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- You've been scarce. The board noticed. So did I.
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- Afternoon. Three jobs closed on the board. Two of them yours. Keep going.
? tier>=colleague time:morning
- Morning. Tea's made. Not by me. I don't take a break. Have mine.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Good. I need someone who listens before they lift a spanner.
? tier>=close
- {me}. Sit. Five minutes. The board can wait five minutes. Don't tell it.   #warm

== bye
- Back to it.
? tier>=friend
- Go on. Good work today. Same again tomorrow.   #warm
?
- Carry on. Finish what you started.
? act:work
- Board's there. Pick the next one.
? time:evening
- Go and eat. Then sleep. In that order.

== feel
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Every fan on Deck 5 at the right pitch. I stood and listened. Two whole minutes.
? mood:ok
- Board's at eleven. Nothing loud. Nothing quiet that should be loud.
? mood:low tier>=colleague
- Long one. I'll sleep on it. Then I'll fix it.

== near
? act:work tier>=acquaintance
- Seal kit's on the left of the bench. Always the left. Put it back there.
? act:dinner tier>=colleague
- Sit. You eat, I'll read the logs. That counts as company.   #funny
? act:breakfast
- Tea. Toast. Board. In that order, every day.
? act:gym
- I walk. Every deck, every vent. That's my gym.
? place:worksbay
- Hear that pump? It's fine. I like to listen anyway. You should too.
? act:leisure
- I'm not working. I'm reading the maintenance logs. That's different.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Every machine on the Wren has a serial number. I know them. Ask me one.
? tier>=colleague
- Torres has good hands. I've told him. Once. That's plenty.
- Nobody thanks the air. That's how you know it's working. Remember that one.
? tier>=friend
- I gave up tea breaks. There's always one more job on the board. Don't copy me.

== invite
? tier>=colleague
- Works tea on Friday. You'll be there. That's not a question.
? trad:today tier>=colleague
- {trad} tonight. I'll look in for ten minutes. You can find me there.

== accept
- Fine. Ten minutes.
- Agreed. I'll be there on time. Be early.
? tier>=friend
- Yes. I'd like that. Don't make it a thing.   #warm

== decline
- Not tonight. Board's at fourteen.
- Can't. Ask me next week. I'll mean it.
? weekday:sat|sun
- It's my day off. I'm going to listen to a fan for an hour. Alone.   #funny

== missed
- You missed our time. Book another. I'll keep it.
- Ten minutes I waited. That's fine once. Book another.
? tier>=friend
- You missed it. Is everything all right? Say if it isn't.

== hint
- Have you got ten minutes? Off the board. Not about work.
- When you're done, come and find me. It isn't a job.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Someone said it's your birthday. I've written it down. I won't remember.   #funny
- Your birthday. Fine. Take the easy job. Just today.
? birthday:me
- It's not my birthday. Who told you. Kovac. It was Kovac.   #funny
- A card on my desk. Signed by Works. I'm keeping it. Don't tell them.   #warm

== week1
? week1:true
- First week. Nobody expects you to be fast. I expect you to be right.
? week1:true mem:intro.dinner
- You ate something on Sunday. Good. Keep doing that.   #funny
? week1:true weekday:mon
- Briefing's done. You're with Torres. Watch his hands, not his mouth.
? week1:true weekday:tue
- Your first job's mine. Glass office, quarter to eight. I'll pick it. You'll do it.
- Rina has you at two. Health check. Go. It isn't optional.
? week1:true weekday:wed
- Pick your own job today. Read the whole card. Then pick.
? week1:true weekday:thu
- Torres is off. Board's yours. Questions come to me.
? week1:true weekday:fri
- Works tea at half ten. Bring your hands. There's a mug for you.
